# script-rules.list — rules template for check-script-preflight.
# gate-sdk/SPEC.md §check-script-preflight. Copy to your gates dir as
# script-rules.list, name your scripts in GATE_SDK_SCRIPT_FILES, and uncomment
# the blocks you want, each bound to your own commands, paths and grammars.
#
# A block opens with 'rule <ID> <kind>' and takes the indented '<key> <value>'
# lines after it; '#' lines and blank lines are ignored. An ERE value is a search,
# so anchor it with ^ and $ to match the whole text. A site a rule cannot see is
# cleared by '# <waiver>: <reason>' on any physical line of its logical line.

# The shortest waiver reason, in characters; the default is 1.
# waiver-min 10

# Commands whose here-doc or quoted operand is read as a script of its own.
# body sbatch

# command: every invocation of cmd is refused unless an allow ERE matches its
# text, a before ERE matches the code ahead of it on its line, or a waiver clears it.
# rule KILL-BY-PARENT command
#   cmd pkill
#   allow ^pkill -P "[$][A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*"$
#   before ^timeout [0-9]+ $
#   waiver kill-ok

# forbidden-token: a line's code holding any token is refused.
# rule SHARED-MOUNT forbidden-token
#   token /mnt/shared
#   waiver mount-ok

# early-exit: a reader that stops early, fed under pipefail.
# rule PIPEFAIL-READER early-exit
#   waiver pipefail-ok

# id-grammar: each listed flag's value in an invocation of cmd must match grammar.
# rule OWNER-ID id-grammar
#   cmd submit
#   flag --owner
#   grammar ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{2,31}$
#   waiver owner-ok
